# repositories/
#
# Data access layer — one file per Firestore collection.
# Each repository:
#   - Exposes typed CRUD methods (get, list, create, update, delete)
#   - Owns the Firestore collection path
#   - Returns domain model types (not raw Firestore DocumentSnapshot)
#   - Handles Firestore Timestamps ↔ string conversion
#
# Stage 2 will add:
#   event.repository.ts       — /events/{eventId}
#   team.repository.ts        — /events/{eventId}/teams/{teamId}
#   checkpoint.repository.ts  — /events/{eventId}/checkpoints/{cpId}
#   user.repository.ts        — /users/{uid}
#   leaderboard.repository.ts — /events/{eventId}/leaderboard/{entryId}
